rominent toggle affecting an entire section or page."],[1894,"**Chart container:** `data-width`, `data-height`, `data-x-labels`, `data-y-labels`, `data-x-labels-vertical`, `data-x-baseline`, `data-y-baseline`, `data-x-tick-marks`, `data-y-tick-marks`"],[634,"**Check browser console**: Look for network errors"],[1773,"**Check container**: Ensure the chart container is not transformed or positioned in a complex layout"],[1768,"**Check data**: Ensure `series` array has data and `xAccessor`/`yAccessor` return valid values"],[1770,"**Check dimensions**: Ensure container has non-zero width and height"],[1769,"**Check domains**: Verify `yDomain` (if set) includes your data values"],[632,"**Check icon name**: Ensure the icon exists in the CDN"],[1772,"**Check scroll position**: The component accounts for horizontal scroll automatically"],[236,"**Checkbox:** `data-selected`, `data-indeterminate`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-disabled`"],[235,"**CheckboxGroup Container:** `data-invalid`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`, `data-readonly`, `data-orientation`"],[618,"**Client-Side Hydration**: The sprite sheet is generated and injected after hydration, causing a brief paint event"],[558,"**Color inheritance**: Uses `currentColor` by default for seamless theme integration"],[1549,"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, `Input` or `TextArea`, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. Omitting `Group` leaves the control as a direct field child with box chrome. Use an explicit `Group` for controls or adornments"],[495,"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `DatePickerCalendar`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in. `children` also accepts a function for picker state"],[1221,"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `SelectOptions`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"],[880,"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, the control, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"],[1223,"**Composed in another field**: Use `variant=\"control\"` to sit inside another field's `Group`, as a country-code select beside a phone `Input`"],[728,"**Composes into other components**: `Select` uses `ListBox` internally; reach for `ListBox` directly when you need an inline list rather than a popover dropdown."],[629,"**Consider preloading** frequently used icons to reduce loading delays"],[726,"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` for controlled state, or `defaultSelectedKeys` for uncontrolled."],[884,"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"],[1225,"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"],[1552,"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"],[1522,"**Controls keep the scale size.** A `Button` inside a lockup follows the surrounding\n`SizeProvider` or its own `size` prop, never the lockup's tier."],[1551,"**Controls**: A `Button slot=\"control\"` beside the input is an interactive affix; it picks up field chrome from context"],[1931,"**Custom Components:** When using `as={MyComponent}`, Box accepts that component's props. If there's a prop name conflict, Box's props take priority."],[1716,"**Custom domains**: Set explicit x and y ranges for controlled scales across multiple charts"],[1715,"**Customizable axes**: Control gridlines, tick marks, axis titles, and tick formatting"],[1777,"**Debounce resize**: The default 15ms debounce on `useParentSize` balances smoothness and performance"],[617,"**Deduplication**: Icon path data only exists once in the sprite sheet, regardless of how many times it's used"],[1713,"**Design system alignment**: 8px border radius, 12px bar width (1.5 GU), consistent spacing"],[619,"**DOM Output:**"],[1622,"**End**"],[564,"**Events**: `onClick`, `onMouseOver`, `onFocus`, etc."],[1517,"**Every part names its role with a slot**: `eyebrow`, `title`, `body`. Unslotted text follows\nthe lockup's tier too: a bare `Heading` takes the title tier and a bare `Text` the body tier."],[635,"**Fallback content**: Provide placeholder content for loading states"],[623,"**Faster Rendering**: Browser optimizations for `<use>` elements"],[608,"**First Request**: When an icon is first encountered, it triggers an asynchronous fetch from the CDN"],[557,"**Flexible sizing**: Support for `width` and `height` props"],[1228,"**Form integration**: Set `name` and the value submits as part of a native `<form>` (multiple values submit as repeated entries)"],[611,"**Full SVG Rendering**: Each icon instance renders as a complete SVG element with all path data"],[1736,"**Group gap**: Minimum 24px between bar groups"],[1748,"**Grouped rendering**: Bars are rendered in SVG `<Group>` elements for logical organization"],[1620,"**Home**"],[1751,"**Horizontal charts**: Vertical scrolling when many categories exceed container height"],[1740,"**Horizontal scrolling**: When data points exceed available width, the chart becomes horizontally scrollable"],[1930,"**HTML Elements:** When using `as=\"button\"`, TypeScript enforces button-specific props like `type`, `disabled`, and `onClick`."],[1921,"**Important**: Since `Flex` and `Grid` extend `Box`, prefer them for layouts. Use `Box` only when you need a non-flex, non-grid container."],[586,"**Important**: When you supply a `className`, you make a commitment to take over all styling of the component as it will remove the standard class names. Use data attributes for targeted styling instead."],[626,"**Initial Flash**: Brief moment where icons appear/disappear during sprite injection"],[1714,"**Interactive tooltips**: Hover to see exact values, with smart positioning and scroll-awareness"],[241,"**isInvalid**: Shows error state styling"],[240,"**isRequired**: Marks the group as required with visual indicator"],[1743,"**Keyboard navigation**: Bar groups are keyboard accessible with `tabIndex={0}` and `role=\"group\"`"],[727,"**Layout primitive**: `ListBox` and `ListBoxItem` accept layout props (`gap`, `padding`, etc.) — they extend `FlexOwnProps`."],[1639,"**Left** — when the group controls content directly below or within the same column (dashboards, tables)."],[1776,"**Limit data points**: Consider pagination or filtering for very large datasets (>100 points)"],[622,"**Lower Memory Usage**: Especially beneficial with many repeated icons"],[1738,"**Margins**: 20px top/right, 60px bottom/left for axes and labels"],[639,"**Minimize icon sets**: Only load icons that are actually used"],[1742,"**Minimum spacing**: Group gaps never fall below 24px, triggering scroll instead"],[1553,"**Multiline**: Compose a `TextArea` instead of an `Input` for multiline entry"],[633,"**Network connectivity**: Verify CDN is accessible"],[1017,"**No step is highlighted:** `currentStep` is omitted, negative, or out of range. Set it to the active step's 0-based index."],[555,"**On-demand loading**: Icons are loaded asynchronously from CDN only when needed"],[620,"**Performance Benefits:**"],[637,"**Preload common icons**: Consider preloading frequently used icons"],[630,"**Provide fallback content** for critical icons to handle loading states"],[1062,"**Radio Button:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-disabled`"],[1061,"**RadioGroup Container:** `data-invalid`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`, `data-readonly`, `data-orientation`"],[729,"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria ListBox for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead."],[1229,"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria Select for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead"],[1958,"**Recommended default**: Use `Flex` for most layouts. Since it extends `Box`, you get all `Box` capabilities without needing to nest components."],[621,"**Reduced DOM Size**: Path data stored once instead of duplicated"],[616,"**Reference Rendering**: Each icon renders as a lightweight `<use>` element that references the sprite"],[1712,"**Responsive behavior**: Auto-sizing with horizontal scrolling for many data points, sticky axes"],[1749,"**Responsive sizing**: `useParentSize` hook provides efficient resize detection with debouncing (15ms)"],[1641,"**Right** — when the group represents utility or contextual controls (e.g. grid/list view toggle)."],[1717,"**RTL support*&#x2A;: Full right-to-left layout support for international audiences &#x2A;(in development)*"],[1747,"**Scales**: VisX's `scaleBand` and `scaleLinear` for efficient coordinate mapping"],[1744,"**Screen reader support**: Semantic HTML structure with proper ARIA attributes"],[1188,"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"],[1189,"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1276,"**Shared structural containers.** These generic, layout-only components are the building blocks for composing a component's interior (a `Modal`, a card, a panel). They are semantic containers built on `Flex`, so they accept the same layout props (`direction`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `padding`, ...)."],[246,"**Shift + Tab**: Moves focus to the previous checkbox"],[1778,"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"],[1710,"**Single and multi-series support**: Display one or multiple data series with grouped bars"],[1224,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"],[725,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"single\"` or `\"multiple\"`."],[497,"**Sizes**: Each picker is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, trigger, description, error, and the calendar it opens; without it, the picker follows the surrounding scope"],[1555,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, description, error, and composed controls; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope. An explicit `size` on a part still wins for that part"],[882,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, steppers, description, and error; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope"],[1227,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"],[1618,"**Space / Enter**"],[1067,"**Space**: Select the focused radio button"],[245,"**Space**: Toggles the focused checkbox"],[773,"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"],[1192,"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"],[615,"**Sprite Sheet Creation**: A hidden SVG sprite sheet is automatically injected into the DOM containing symbol definitions"],[625,"**SSR Limitation**: Sprite references render empty until client-side hydration"],[1283,"**Standalone** - with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."],[881,"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon and `variant=\"control\"` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"],[1752,"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"],[1741,"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"],[565,"**Styling**: `className`, `style`, `data-*` attributes"],[609,"**SVG Parsing**: The fetched SVG string is parsed into a React element using `@bento/svg-parser`"],[1614,"**Tab**"],[244,"**Tab**: Moves focus to the next/previous checkbox"],[1064,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the radio group"],[1190,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"],[1520,"**The body is `<Text slot=\"body\">`**, once or as many times as the copy needs."],[1518,"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."],[1519,"**The title is `<Heading slot=\"title\">`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the\nvisual size: `size` handles the visuals, so `level={1}` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."],[1019,"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."],[1610,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1609,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[1756,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[1745,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[624,"**Trade-offs:**"],[566,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[496,"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1222,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[776,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[1932,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[560,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1719,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1996,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[627,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[628,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[638,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[885,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1226,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1554,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[883,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1774,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1711,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1750,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1720,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[614,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1340,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1337,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1346,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1347,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1335,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1341,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1344,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1338,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1350,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[154,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[1975,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1977,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1971,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[1973,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[1978,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[1974,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[1972,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[1976,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[1928,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[454,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1513,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1070,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1195,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[354,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[247,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1071,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1196,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[249,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1073,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1626,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1197,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[353,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[971,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[248,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1072,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[351,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[969,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[968,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[350,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[970,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[352,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1920,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[153,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[1731,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[233,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[303,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[321,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[299,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[314,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1668,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1888,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1005,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[589,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[592,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[588,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[590,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[591,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[593,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1328,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[498,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1478,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[374,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[468,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1469,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1477,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[943,"`Enter/Space`"],[416,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[683,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[383,"`Escape`"],[857,"`Escape`"],[945,"`Escape`"],[1673,"`Escape`"],[453,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1957,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[597,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1995,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[470,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[671,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[700,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1871,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[471,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[1926,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[730,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1925,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[765,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[501,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[850,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[845,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1004,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1723,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1397,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1663,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[691,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[674,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[937,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[677,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[915,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[920,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes